$\quad$ Number of electrons per kg of silver

$$

=\frac{6.023 \times 10^{26}}{108}

$$

Number of electrons per unit volume of silver

$$

\begin{array}{c}

n=\frac{6.023 \times 10^{26}}{108} \times 10.5 \times 10^{3} \\

\qquad \begin{array}{c}

v_{d}=\frac{I}{n e A} \\

=\frac{20}{6.023 \times 10^{26} \times 10.5 \times 10^{3} \times 1.6 \times 10^{-19} \times 3.14 \times 10^{-6}} \times 108 \\

=6.798 \times 10^{-4} \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{sec} .

\end{array}

\end{array}

$$
